Id: path011w
Severity: WARN
Category: accounts
Check: check_path
Controls: CIS 4.1; NIST CM-6; ISO 8.9; CE Secure configuration

A directory on a user's PATH is not owned by that user. Another account
can then replace the programs in it with Trojan horses that run under
the user's identity the next time they type the command name. Give the
directory to the user whose PATH names it, or take it out of the PATH.

It is a WARN when the file named is executable, or when the owner
expected is not root.

Until 3.4.0 this was reported as path006; the number changed because
path006w meant something else in older versions.
